    "final_message": "Here's my recommendation for your Monday in Paris:\n\n## 🏆 Recommended: New Asiaway\n\nOut of the four Chinese restaurants in Paris, **New Asiaway** best fits all your criteria and has the highest rating:\n\n| Detail | Info |\n|--------|------|\n| **Restaurant** | New Asiaway |\n| **Rating** | ⭐ 4.6/5 (highest of the four Chinese restaurants) |\n| **Address** | 123 Rue de la Gaite, 75014 Paris, France |\n| **Price per person** | €30 (under your €34 budget ✓) |\n| **Operating hours** | 12:00 PM – 3:00 PM, 6:00 PM – 10:00 PM |\n| **Open Monday?** | ✅ Yes |\n\n**What reviewers say:**\n> \"Authentic Chinese cuisine with a modern twist. Fresh ingredients and flavorful sauces. Attentive and knowledgeable staff. Great ambiance and stylish decor. The restaurant has a great selection of wines and the food was delicious.\"\n\n**Note on alternatives:** Two other options also fit your budget and are open Mondays — *The yard* (4.3 rating, €30/person) and *China Garden* (4.4 rating, though I couldn't retrieve its exact price). However, New Asiaway clearly wins on ratings and reviews. *Royal Panda* isn't open on Mondays, so it's out.\n\nWould you like me to make a reservation for Monday? If so, just let me know what time you'd prefer (lunch 12–3 PM or dinner 6–10 PM)! 🍜",
